# Hello Butler — Dev & Deployment Hand Note

## Environment

DEV:
`.env.dev`

PROD:
`.env.production`

Never commit either.

`.gitignore`:
`.env`
`.env.*`
`!.env.example`


# Architecture

DEV:
`Local FastAPI :8001 → Docker Postgres :5433 → DEV volume`

PROD:
`Internet → Cloudflare → localhost:8000 → Docker Backend → Docker Postgres :5432 → PROD volume`

Same `postgres:16` image, separate Compose projects/containers/volumes.


# DEV — Start PostgreSQL

From repo root:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-dev --env-file .env.dev up -d postgres`

Check:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-dev --env-file .env.dev ps`

Logs:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-dev --env-file .env.dev logs -f postgres`

Stop:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-dev --env-file .env.dev down`

DEV volume:
`hello-butler-dev_postgres_data`


# DEV — Run Backend

VS Code / Uvicorn args:

    "args": [
        "app.main:app",
        "--host",
        "127.0.0.1",
        "--port",
        "8001",
        "--env-file",
        "../.env.dev"
    ]

Backend:
`http://localhost:8001`

Swagger:
`http://localhost:8001/docs`


# DEV — Alembic

From `backend/`:

Upgrade:

`uv run --env-file ../.env.dev alembic upgrade head`

Check:

`uv run --env-file ../.env.dev alembic current`


# PROD — Build

From repo root:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production build backend`

Or build + start:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production up -d --build`

Rebuild when:
- source code changes
- dependencies change
- Dockerfile changes

NO rebuild for:
- `.env.production` changes
- normal `compose.yaml` config changes


# PROD — Alembic

Upgrade:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production run --rm backend uv run --no-sync alembic upgrade head`

Check:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production run --rm backend uv run --no-sync alembic current`


# PROD — Start

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production up -d`

Check:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production ps`

Logs:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production logs -f backend`

Stop:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production down`

Never use `down -v` unless intentionally deleting DB data.

PROD volume:
`hello-butler-prod_postgres_data`


# PROD — Env Changed Only

Recreate backend:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production up -d --no-deps --force-recreate backend`

No rebuild required.


# PROD — New Code From main

`git checkout main`

`git pull`

Build:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production build backend`

Migrate:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production run --rm backend uv run --no-sync alembic upgrade head`

Deploy:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production up -d`

Verify:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production ps`

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production logs --tail 100 backend`


# Docker — Useful

Running:

`docker ps`

All containers:

`docker ps -a`

Images:

`docker images`

Volumes:

`docker volume ls`

Compose resolved config:

`docker compose -p hello-butler-prod --env-file .env.production config`

WARNING: `config` prints resolved secrets. Do not share its output.


# Docker Restart

In `compose.yaml`:

`restart: unless-stopped`

Used for:
- backend
- postgres

Container crash → restart
Docker restart → restart
Manual stop → stays stopped


# Cloudflare — Quick Tunnel

Production backend must be running on:

`http://localhost:8000`

Start temporary tunnel:

`cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:8000`

Returns:

`https://xxxxx.trycloudflare.com`

Test:

`https://xxxxx.trycloudflare.com/docs`

Keep terminal running.

Quick Tunnel URL changes when recreated.


# Cloudflare — Check

Version:

`cloudflared --version`

Current tested version:
`2026.9.1`


# WSL / Docker Desktop

Check WSL:

`wsl --list`

Expected:
- `Ubuntu-24.04`
- `docker-desktop`

Check Docker engine:

`docker ps`

Docker Desktop manages its own `docker-desktop` WSL distribution.


# Ports

`8000` → PROD backend / Cloudflare

`8001` → DEV backend

`5432` → PostgreSQL inside Docker network

`5433` → DEV PostgreSQL exposed to Windows


# Database Addresses

DEV local backend:

`localhost:5433`

PROD Docker backend:

`postgres:5432`


# Env Relationship

`.env.dev`
→ DEV Postgres config
→ DEV FastAPI config

`.env.production`
→ PROD Postgres config
→ PROD Docker backend config

Compose `${VAR}` requires:

`--env-file .env.dev`

or:

`--env-file .env.production`

Backend Docker also receives production env through:

    env_file:
      - ./.env.production


# Production Deployment Flow

`main`
↓
`build image`
↓
`alembic upgrade head`
↓
`docker compose up -d`
↓
`check ps`
↓
`check logs`
↓
`health test`
↓
`Cloudflare → production :8000`


# DON'T

Don't commit `.env.dev` / `.env.production`.

Don't use PROD DB for development.

Don't run DEV backend on `8000`.

Don't use `docker compose down -v` on PROD.

Don't expose/share `docker compose config` output.

Don't rebuild image for env-only changes.


